{"id":"kolu-ci-root","ord":"a0","title":"kolu-ci — the Incus pool venue","desc":"The CI venue's own page: the pool of Incus containers (kolu-ci-*) odu runs dispatch to over ssh (reached via a 127.0.0.1 proxy device, user toor). Downtimes and venue incidents are filed under `downtimes`, evidence-first, for the Incus admin.","created":"2026-08-29T14:22:59-04:00"}
{"id":"kolu-ci-downtimes","parent":"kolu-ci-root","ord":"a0","title":"downtimes","desc":"One child per incident: what died, when (UTC and ET), what was running, the exact client-side symptom, and what the host itself says. For the Incus admin.","created":"2026-08-29T14:22:59-04:00"}
{"id":"downtime-2026-08-29a","parent":"kolu-ci-downtimes","ord":"a0","title":"kolu-ci-9: the ssh connection died mid-run; the whole run was lost","date":"2026-08-29","desc":"At about 15:28 UTC (11:28 ET), while olai PR #427's CI was running on kolu-ci-9, the ssh connection to the container dropped two minutes into the e2e tests. The whole run was lost, because the odu coordinator of that era crashed when a transport died under it. The children carry the exact error and what we know of the cause.","created":"2026-08-29T14:22:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T16:05:46-04:00","custom":{"host":"kolu-ci-9"}}
{"id":"downtime-2026-08-29b","parent":"kolu-ci-downtimes","ord":"a1","title":"kolu-ci-9: the same ssh death, two hours later","date":"2026-08-29","desc":"At about 17:34 UTC (13:34 ET), the same container dropped its ssh connection again — also in the middle of the e2e tests, this time during olai PR #428's CI. Everything that had already finished stayed green; only the in-flight e2e errored. A fresh run on the pool immediately after passed 10/10, so the failure does not follow the code. The children carry the error and the cause reading.","created":"2026-08-29T14:22:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T16:05:46-04:00","custom":{"host":"kolu-ci-9"}}
{"id":"downtime-2026-08-29-hostprobe","parent":"kolu-ci-downtimes","ord":"a2","title":"the host's testimony: kolu-ci-9 never rebooted — the ssh path broke, not the container","date":"2026-08-29","desc":"Probed at 18:21 UTC, after both incidents, over the same ssh path that had failed: the container had been up for six days (since Aug 22 — through BOTH incident windows), never rebooted, load under 1, and 103 of 125 GiB memory free. So neither incident was a container crash or memory pressure — the machine sailed through both. The break is between us and it. The probe's exact output:\n\n```\nkolu-ci-9\n 18:21:59  up 6 days 22:09,  0 users,  load average: 0.78, 0.55, 0.67\nreboot   system boot  6.12.85   Sat Aug 22 20:12   still running\nMem: 125Gi total, 103Gi free\n```","created":"2026-08-29T14:22:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T16:05:46-04:00","custom":{"host":"kolu-ci-9"}}
{"id":"dt829a-error","parent":"downtime-2026-08-29a","ord":"a0","title":"the error, exactly as the client saw it","desc":"Every log subscription errored at the same moment. The transcript: `⚠ errored e2e@x86_64-linux 2m19s`, then eight `logTail: append … after its log ended` throws, then Bun's crash footer. The full transcript is preserved in briefs/odu-teardown-crash.md (the investigation that followed).","created":"2026-08-31T16:05:46-04:00"}
{"id":"dt829a-cause","parent":"downtime-2026-08-29a","ord":"a1","title":"root cause — half found and fixed, half still with the admin","desc":"Two layers. The CLIENT half — the coordinator crashing when the transport died — was root-caused and fixed the same day: juspay/odu#93 (merged 17:31 UTC), after which a dying transport errors one node instead of killing the run. The HOST half — why the ssh connection dropped at all — is still unexplained: the container itself never died (see `downtime-2026-08-29-hostprobe` — up since Aug 22, healthy through both incidents), so the break is somewhere in the ssh path: the Incus proxy device forwarding 127.0.0.1, the pool host's network, or a timeout that kills long-lived busy ssh streams. The system journal from the incident window needs the admin's eyes — the unprivileged `toor` user cannot read it.","created":"2026-08-31T16:05:46-04:00"}
{"id":"dt829b-error","parent":"downtime-2026-08-29b","ord":"a0","title":"the error, exactly as the client saw it","desc":"The lane's transport died mid-e2e (the odu#93 fix had not merged yet at this run's start, but only the one node errored this time). The CI watcher's classification, verbatim: \"a dead lane host — not master drift, not a code fix to make.\" The retry (seq 2) went 10/10 on the pool.","created":"2026-08-31T16:05:46-04:00"}
{"id":"dt829b-cause","parent":"downtime-2026-08-29b","ord":"a1","title":"root cause — the same suspect as the first incident","desc":"The container stayed up and healthy through this incident too (see `downtime-2026-08-29-hostprobe`). The pattern that points the finger: both drops hit kolu-ci-9, both during the e2e leg — the longest and most network-chatty node — roughly two hours apart. The suspect is the ssh path under a long-lived busy stream, not the machine. Unconfirmed until the admin reads the sshd and kernel logs from the two windows.","created":"2026-08-31T16:05:46-04:00"}
